		text-decoration-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ink) 30%, transparent);
		text-underline-offset: 4px;
	}

	.wall-head nav a:hover {
		text-decoration-color: var(--thread);
		text-decoration-thickness: 2.5px;
	}

	/* ---- the head on a narrow wall: same objects, less air ---------- */
	/* A THIRD OF THE PHONE'S FIRST SCREEN WAS CHROME CARRYING NO CANDIDATE
	   FACT. Measured at 390 × 844, root 16, identical in both locales: this
	   block ran 277.3px — 32.8 % of the viewport — and the first fact about
	   the man, his own name, arrived at y 348, i.e. 41.2 % of the one screen
	   that decides whether the other 25 get read. The desktop wall pays 165px
	   of 900 (18.3 %) for the same five links and the same language chit, so
	   the phone was paying more than twice the toll on the surface where
	   space is scarcest, and those 348px displaced exactly the two lines that
	   name a technology and state the ask.
	   WHAT IS NOT DONE HERE, and it was proposed: dropping the five-link
	   directory on phone entirely, on the grounds that the rail carries the
	   same five destinations. It buys 102px and it costs more than that.
	   The rail's names are `clip-path`-hidden at rest — only the CURRENT
	   district prints — so five labelled controls would be traded for five
